{
  "$comment": [
    "Per-component versions for the slides surface. The plugin version tells someone the PLUGIN is",
    "stale; this tells them which of the components THEY used actually changed, which is the only",
    "thing that makes them act. Bump a component's version in the same commit that changes its spec",
    "— scripts/check-drift.sh reads this file and a build's stamp, and reports the intersection.",
    "",
    "version = the plugin version in which that component's spec last changed.",
    "breaking = true when a build using it will render WRONG until updated, as opposed to merely",
    "missing an improvement. It is the difference between a red notice and an amber one.",
    "",
    "Every entry is seeded at 1.45.0 because this surface is new — there are no earlier slide",
    "builds for a bump to warn, so there is nothing to over-report.",
    "",
    "`source` records where each spec came from, because they are not equally reliable:",
    "  figma   — read off node properties in GW-Slides. Authoritative (R0).",
    "  export  — derived from the Google Slides .pptx shape tree, doubled to 1920x1080. Good,",
    "            but Slides re-fits text, so type is the weak spot.",
    "  authored — built from tokens because no source has it. A first draft, not a spec.",
    "An `authored` entry that later gets measured is a BREAKING bump: builds made against the",
    "draft will be wrong, not merely dated."
  ],
